<article class="env-definition" id="09P2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09P2">Definition <span data-tag="09P2">22.25.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a graded category over $R$. A direct sum $(x, y, z, i, j, p, q)$ in $\mathcal{A}$ (notation as in Homology, Remark <a href="/tag/0103" data-tag="0103">12.3.6</a>) is a <em>graded direct sum</em> if $i, j, p, q$ are homogeneous of degree $0$. </p>
</article>